  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 232 PM EDT Sun Sep 6 2026\n\n- Chances for Rain late Tuesday into Wednesday and again next \n  weekend\n\nFair weather continues through Labor Day into most of Tuesday.\nThere could be some shallow fog late tonight into early Monday \nmorning as light winds and clear skies result in radiational\ncooling. Lows will drop into the upper 40s and lower 50s by\ndaybreak across much of the forecast area.\n\nAn Omega block across the CONUS breaks down early this week as a \nlow across the Pacific NW kicks east and flattens the upper high, \nwith surface low pressure tracking across southern Canada. Return \nflow of moisture and a surface cold front should kick off some \nshowers and thunderstorms late Tuesday into Wednesday. Shear \nprofiles suggest organized convection is possible if instability \nis sufficient Tuesday evening ahead of the front.\n\nA zonal flow pattern across the northern CONUS should allow a\nquick progression of a shortwave trough from the Pacific NW into\nthe upper Great Lakes by next weekend with increasing chances for\nshowers and thunderstorms late Friday into Sunday.",
